# Color Usage Rules

1. Warm ivory should be the primary background color.
2. Burgundy should be used for important calls to action.
3. Gold should be used sparingly as an accent.
4. Body text should use rich brown or charcoal.
5. White should be used where maximum contrast is required.
6. Light gold text should not appear on cream backgrounds.
7. All color combinations must be tested for accessibility.

