# Typography

The website should use no more than three primary font roles.

## Heading Font

A refined serif font should be used for:

- Page titles
- Section headings
- Book titles
- Featured quotations

Possible choices:

- Cormorant Garamond
- Playfair Display
- Libre Baskerville

## Body Font

A highly readable sans-serif font should be used for:

- Paragraphs
- Navigation
- Product information
- Recipe instructions
- Forms

Possible choices:

- Inter
- Source Sans 3
- Lato

## Accent Font

A restrained script font may be used for:

- Short decorative phrases
- Selected taglines
- Signature-style text

Script fonts should never be used for long paragraphs, buttons, or essential instructions.

---

# Typography Scale

| Style | Suggested Size |
|---|---:|
| Display heading | 56–72 px |
| Page heading | 40–48 px |
| Section heading | 30–36 px |
| Card heading | 22–26 px |
| Body text | 16–18 px |
| Small text | 14 px |
| Button text | 15–17 px |

Typography must scale responsively on mobile devices.

---

# Spacing System

Use an eight-pixel spacing system.

| Token | Size |
|---|---:|
| `space-1` | 4 px |
| `space-2` | 8 px |
| `space-3` | 16 px |
| `space-4` | 24 px |
| `space-5` | 32 px |
| `space-6` | 48 px |
| `space-7` | 64 px |
| `space-8` | 96 px |

Consistent spacing should be used instead of selecting random values for each page.

---

# Layout Principles

1. Design mobile-first.
2. Use generous white space.
3. Keep paragraphs at a comfortable reading width.
4. Avoid overcrowding pages with too many product categories.
5. Use clear visual hierarchy.
6. Keep primary actions easy to identify.
7. Maintain consistent margins and section spacing.
8. Use responsive grids for products, recipes, books, and videos.

---

# Buttons

## Primary Button

Use for the most important action on a page.

Examples:

- Shop the Book
- Explore the Library
- Read the Recipe
- Subscribe

Suggested appearance:

- Burgundy background
- White text
- Rounded corners
- Clear hover and focus states

## Secondary Button

Use for supporting actions.

Suggested appearance:

- Transparent or ivory background
- Burgundy border
- Burgundy text

## Text Link

Use for simple navigation or supporting information.

Links must remain visually recognizable and should not rely only on color.

---

# Cards

Reusable cards may be created for:

- Books
- Recipes
- Videos
- Shopify products
- Articles
- Website rooms

Every card should include:

- A clear image
- A descriptive title
- Short supporting text
- A clear action
- Accessible alternative text
- Consistent spacing

---

# Images

## Image Style

Images should feel:

- Authentic
- Warmly lit
- Inviting
- Countryside-inspired
- Detailed but not cluttered
- Consistent with the Lady Amour brand

## Preferred Images

- Real food photography
- Real product photography
- Countryside landscapes
- Gardens and mountains
- Books in comfortable reading settings
- Tea, wood fire, flowers, linen, and rustic tables
- Lifestyle photographs of Amour S.

## Image Rules

1. Use original photography whenever possible.
2. Avoid visibly artificial food imagery.
3. Do not stretch or distort photographs.
4. Use responsive image sizes.
5. Compress images for website performance.
6. Add meaningful alternative text.
7. Maintain consistent image aspect ratios within grids.

---

# Iconography

Icons should be simple, elegant, and easy to understand.

Initial room icons:

- Library — book
- Atelier — artist tools or needle and thread
- Fireside — flame
- Cellar — jar or bottle
- Apothecary — leaf or mortar and pestle
- Home — house
- Garden — flower
- Vlogs — video camera

Icons should support labels rather than replace them.

---

# Forms

Forms should include:

- Visible labels
- Clear instructions
- Accessible error messages
- Keyboard support
- Strong focus indicators
- Confirmation messages
- Appropriate input types

Forms should not rely only on placeholder text.

---

# Accessibility Standards

The website should aim to meet WCAG 2.2 Level AA.

Requirements include:

- Sufficient color contrast
- Keyboard navigation
- Visible focus indicators
- Semantic HTML
- Alternative text
- Form labels
- Captions for video content
- Reduced-motion support
- Responsive text
- Touch-friendly controls

---

# Motion and Animation

Animations should feel slow, graceful, and purposeful.

Preferred effects:

- Gentle fades
- Subtle zooms
- Soft page transitions
- Small hover movements

Avoid:

- Rapid flashing
- Excessive movement
- Spinning elements
- Distracting animations
- Motion that prevents users from reading content

Users who prefer reduced motion should receive a simplified experience.

---

# Responsive Breakpoints

Initial working breakpoints:

| Device | Width |
|---|---:|
| Small mobile | Below 480 px |
| Mobile | 480–767 px |
| Tablet | 768–1023 px |
| Desktop | 1024–1439 px |
| Large desktop | 1440 px and above |

Breakpoints may be adjusted during development based on the content.

